    "text": "A TCP Connection > TCP is connection-oriented as it establishes a virtual path between the source and destination. > All segments belonging to a message are then sent over this virtual path. > TCP uses services of IP to deliver individual segments to receiver, but it controls the connection itself. > Ifa segment is lost/corrupted, it 1s retransmitted. IP 1s unaware of this retransmission. > If asegment arrives out of order; TCP holds it until missing segments arrive; IP is unaware of this too. In TCP, connection-oriented transmission requites three phases: = r 1.- connection establishment a a Bp ~ L oO 2.. data transfer HK) —@—{R) 3. _ connection termination Ry Ry R",
